-- title:
--   Frobenius kernels of a connected p-divisible group have order pⁿᵈ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $h_0$ a natural number, and let $H$ be a family of types indexed by $v\in\mathbb N$, each $H_v$ a commutative ring which is a Hopf algebra over $\mathbb F_p=\mathbb Z/p$ with cocommutative comultiplication and finite as an $\mathbb F_p$-module. Assume given bialgebra maps $s_v\colon H_{v+1}\to H_v$ over $\mathbb F_p$, each surjective, such that $\dim_{\mathbb F_p} H_v=p^{v h_0}$ for all $v$, and such that for every $v$ the kernel of $s_v$ is the ideal $\mathrm{torsionIdeal}(H_{v+1},p^v)$, namely the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon)\subseteq H_{v+1}$ under the algebra endomorphism $[p^v]$ obtained as the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity; assume moreover that each $H_v$ is a local ring. Let $n\le w$ be natural numbers. Then the quotient of $H_w$ by the ideal generated by $\{a^{p^n}: a\in\ker(\varepsilon_{H_w})\}$ has $\mathbb F_p$-dimension $$\dim_{\mathbb F_p}\bigl(H_w/(a^{p^n}:a\in\ker\varepsilon)\bigr)=p^{\,n\,d},\qquad d=\dim_{\mathbb F_p}\bigl(I_1/I_1^2\bigr),$$ where $I_1=\ker(\varepsilon_{H_1})$ is the augmentation ideal of $H_1$ and $I_1/I_1^2$ is its cotangent module.
--
--   This is the order count for the Frobenius kernels of a connected $p$-divisible group over $\mathbb F_p$, presented for an explicit tower of local Hopf algebras: the $n$-th Frobenius kernel of the tower has order $p^{nd}$, with $d$ the dimension of the cotangent space at the origin of the first layer. It is used to identify the quotient $H_w/(a^{p^n}:a\in\ker\varepsilon)$ with a truncated polynomial algebra, in [`PDivisibleGroup.ker_aeval_quotient_span_pow_augIdeal_eq_span_X_pow_of_isLocalRing`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.ker_aeval_quotient_span_pow_augIdeal_eq_span_X_pow_of_isLocalRing).
